    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (73.35) and **Yordan Alvarez** (68.01) headlining our offensive attack. **Junior Caminero** occupies the premier spot against Bassitt, benefiting from a +19% bump in SP skill favorability and an elite xwOBA of 0.374, which overrides the park factor penalty. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start; despite a tough matchup against Kirby, his elite xwOBA of 0.464 and top-of-the-order positioning make him immune to standard regression metrics. We are also monitoring **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.57), who earns a strong start on the back of his leadoff role (+10%) against a soft matchup, providing the speed floor we desperately need to chase the scarcity in the SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (36.88), who fell just shy of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" threshold. While he benefits from a park boost, the combination of Jobe\u2019s SP skill and a unfavorable slot at #7 kept him on the bench. Conversely, we are leaning into the high-upside platoons of **Dillon Dingler** (56.65) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (57.45). **Dillon Dingler** captures a massive +14% platoon advantage against Newcomb, while **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** is uniquely positioned to exploit Matz given his +11% SP skill rating and a potential opportunity to run against a slow delivery. \n\nWe remain cautious regarding the top of our order, as both **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** carry \"Lineup Pending\" status against Yamamoto. While **Gary Sanchez** is projected at #3, the matchup against an elite 3.61 xERA pitcher like Yamamoto suppresses his ceiling, making him a marginal play today. We are also keeping a close eye on **Colt Keith** (44.90); while he avoids the bench, his negative platoon split against Newcomb makes him the most volatile asset in today's starting nine. With **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Lars Nootbaar** unavailable, we are essentially running a gauntlet of platoon-heavy matchups that hinge on our ability to generate extra-base hits against mid-rotation arms.",
